# Cargo build output for the unified workspace (#194) — never tracked
# (an untracked target/ would also make release builds stamp -dirty).
# The services/** pattern grandfathers stale per-service target/ dirs
# left behind by checkouts that built before the workspace merge.
/target/
services/**/target/

# Release packaging output (`just package` / scripts/package.sh).
/dist/

# TLA+ / TLC model-checker scratch output (docs/design/storage_gc.tla).
docs/design/states/

# Local secrets — provider API keys for end-to-end LLM testing (never commit).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Claude Code agent scratch — git worktrees and write-tracking. Never
# tracked; ignoring it also keeps the working tree clean so release
# builds stamp a bare commit SHA (not "<sha>-dirty"). One tracked
# exception: .claude/skills/ holds thin per-skill shims that defer to
# the agent-agnostic meta/skills/ (see AGENTS.md and meta/README.md).
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/

# Pinned dev/test tooling fetched by `just install-nats` (#233) — a binary,
# and reproducible from .nats-version, so it is never committed.
/.tools/

# `just ci`'s phase log (scripts/ci-timing.sh, #223). Truncated by each run and
# left behind on purpose: after a killed run it is the only record of where the
# time went. Anchored — every gate anchors the log on {{justfile_directory()}},
# so it is always this one file, never a stray copy in a service directory.
/.ci-timings

# TLC model-checker scratch output
docs/design/committed/states/

# CPython bytecode cache. The repo's Python tooling (scripts/check-links.py,
# scripts/coupling-comment.py) is invoked by `just` targets and CI, and CPython
# writes __pycache__/ beside a script whenever one is imported or compiled.
# Same reason as the entries above: it is reproducible scratch, and leaving it
# untracked-but-not-ignored would make release builds stamp "<sha>-dirty".
__pycache__/

# Per-checkout agent/tool scratch (`gh` device ids and the like). One such
# file was committed by accident (finding E4 of the 2026-09-03 review) and
# removed in the Phase 0 work; nothing under here is ever a source.
.local/

# The dogfood instance's secrets never live in the repo; a local
# validation of ops/dogfood/compose.yml may create them here.
ops/dogfood/.secrets/
